#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.10.rst:8
msgid "Guidedog 1.0.0-beta.10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.10.rst:11
msgid "A guitar part can now show tablature beside its staff: ``\\new TabStaff`` draws the six strings of a guitar in standard tuning with a fret number for each note. Guidedog chooses strings and frets as LilyPond does by default, and ``\\1`` to ``\\6`` name a note's string where we want another."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.10.rst:16
msgid "The tab staff follows LilyPond's default tablature: a TAB clef, fret numbers centered on string lines that break around them so they read in light and dark themes, and no rhythm, which the staff above shows. A tied note is repeated, in parentheses, only at the start of a line. On the staff above, string numbers print as circled digits. Metronome marks now print a note symbol for the beat, and ``\\breathe`` prints a breath mark for singers and players. Time signatures and chord names follow LilyPond's defaults: 4/4 prints as C, 2/2 as cut C, and a G seventh chord as G with a raised 7."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.10.rst:22
msgid "The new practical task `Write a songbook <https://insanai.github.io/guidedog/manual/howto/songbook.html>`_ writes *Mary Had a Little Lamb* for voice, piano and guitar: the tune, two verses, chord names, a two-voice piano part, and the guitar part with tablature, explained step by step for students and built as a website and a book. Every manual edition includes it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.10.rst:25
msgid "Pages also read more evenly: a paragraph keeps its justification and hyphenation when one line is loose beside long inline code, and post lists, cards included, are typeset like the rest of the page. `GDS 0016 <https://insanai.github.io/guidedog/discussions/records/0016-guitar-tablature.html>`_ records the tablature design."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.11.rst:8
msgid "Guidedog 1.0.0-beta.11"
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.11.rst:11
msgid "Editors can now work on Guidedog projects visually beside the source. The new crate ``guidedoc-edit`` maps a reStructuredText or Markdown document to blocks with the spans of their markup and their editable text, read with Guidedog's own readers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.11.rst:16
msgid "Its operations replace a block's text, insert, delete and move blocks, set and remove directive options, and add list items. Each one changes only the bytes it must, reads the result again, and refuses an edit that would not read back as intended, such as text that would close a fence early."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.11.rst:19
msgid "Preview builds now point back to the source: each HTML block carries its byte span in the file it was read from, and each PDF gets a page map that places every block on its page. Every build also writes ``gd-dependencies.json``, which names the files each page and book was made from, so an editor rebuilds only the outputs a change affects. ``guidedog capabilities --json`` reports the formats, builders, directives, roles, extensions and plugins of the executable, from the code it links rather than from a table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.11.rst:23
msgid "This release also fixes a document whose included file is created later, which is now read again, and diagrams drawn with Graphviz 2.42, which no longer carry text from one diagram into the next. `GDS 0017 <https://insanai.github.io/guidedog/discussions/records/0017-source-maps-and-capabilities.html>`_ records the design."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.12.rst:8
msgid "Guidedog 1.0.0-beta.12"
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.12.rst:11
msgid "Applications such as Nisaba can now choose what a build may reach separately from what reaches its output. Confinement controls readable folders, the network, plugins, graph files and music files. Content rules control raw markup and unsafe URLs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.12.rst:17
msgid "The project settings ``raw_content`` and ``unsafe_urls`` each accept ``\"allow\"`` or ``\"omit\"``. A library caller can impose its own rules or supply defaults for rules the project leaves unset. ``--untrusted`` still applies strict confinement and omits both kinds of content."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.12.rst:21
msgid "Confined builds now render Typst diagrams and use project templates and preambles inside their readable folders. They always use the embedded compiler, ignore configured external Typst programs and download no packages. Local intersphinx inventories must also lie inside the readable folders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.12.rst:25
msgid "An image written as ``name.*`` now prefers WebP over JPEG in HTML pages. The PDF book still prefers JPEG, which Typst stores without decoding, so one project can supply an image suited to each output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.12.rst:28
msgid "Long runs of MyST labels now resolve without scanning the remaining labels for every target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.12.rst:30
msgid "`GDS 0018 <https://insanai.github.io/guidedog/discussions/records/0018-confinement-and-content-rules.html>`_ records the design and its library interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.6.rst:8
msgid "Guidedog 1.0.0-beta.6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.6.rst:11
msgid "We can now publish dated articles alongside documentation pages. The new ``guidedog ssg`` commands create drafts, schedule release instants, publish articles and withhold them again. Both reStructuredText and Markdown use the same metadata and build-clock gate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.6.rst:15
msgid "We collect articles with ``.. postlist::`` and enable Atom, RSS and sitemap files through ``[site]`` in ``conf.toml``. A dated article uses the built-in article HTML layout, and ``:pdf: article`` adds a standalone PDF using the shared print theme. Project templates receive publication metadata through ``page.meta``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.6.rst:19
msgid "Release builds exclude drafts, future articles and expired articles before resolving navigation, links and public indices. Preview builds include them for local review. Clock-only changes reuse parsed documents, and successful rebuilds remove artifacts for pages that have become unpublished."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.6.rst:23
msgid "Template dependencies follow the names requested during rendering, including dynamic and optional includes. Changing a template that no document uses leaves document pages cached. Navigation context reads and native calls have their own verifying traces. A 1,000-article benchmark checks cold and incremental work, including unchanged builds and isolated body edits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.6.rst:28
msgid "Named mounts assemble existing projects, language editions, shared assets and PDF books in one publication transaction. The Guidedog website itself now uses those mounts. Generated taxonomy archives and paginated collections share the publication gate and remove obsolete pages on successful rebuilds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.6.rst:32
msgid "Project, journal and research presets provide complete starting sites. Theme archives require an explicit SHA-256 pin, use canonical tree checksums and install atomically. Builds verify installed themes offline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.6.rst:36
msgid "We describe the commands and metadata in the `static publishing guide <https://insanai.github.io/guidedog/manual/howto/static-publishing.html>`_. GDS 0013 specifies the complete implementation and its release qualification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.7.rst:8
msgid "Guidedog 1.0.0-beta.7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.7.rst:11
msgid "We can now select a rich introduction with ``.. more::``. Native postlists and collection templates preserve paragraphs, **emphasis**, links, lists and lead images during the build. The full article retains its complete content in HTML and PDF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.7.rst:17
msgid "We render collection introductions through ``post.excerpt_html`` and native listings through ``.. postlist::`` with ``:excerpts:``. Articles without a boundary keep the plain-text summary fallback. Feeds and description metadata continue to use ``:summary:`` independently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.7.rst:21
msgid "Excerpt links and resources are relative to their destination, including nested taxonomy archives and pagination. Repeated native listings use separate anchor namespaces. References to targets and footnotes beyond the boundary lead to the full article. Listings retain source-scoped reference and asset dependencies, and included-file edits rebuild them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.7.rst:26
msgid "This fixes `issue 3 <https://github.com/insanai/guidedog/issues/3>`_. We describe authoring, templates and Tinkerer migration in the `static publishing guide <https://insanai.github.io/guidedog/manual/howto/static-publishing.html>`_. The release also includes the SSG corrections and custom-directive documentation reviewed after beta.6. Every platform archive exercises rich excerpts in its complete SSG smoke test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.8.rst:8
msgid "Guidedog 1.0.0-beta.8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.8.rst:11
msgid "We can now write Typst drawing source directly in an RST or MyST ``typst-diagram`` directive. Guidedog's embedded compiler generates SVG or PNG and includes it in the website and PDF book. CeTZ and Fletcher use ordinary version-pinned imports, and local helper libraries work without a separate figure-generation task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.8.rst:17
msgid "Diagrams support captions, alternative text, names, classes, alignment and numbered figure references. Imported helpers and data files are tracked by content, and identical generated images keep their timestamps so unchanged books remain cached. The project package and font settings apply to both outputs. Untrusted builds retain source without executing Typst, and image export requires one finite page with bounded PNG dimensions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.8.rst:22
msgid "For network preview we run ``guidedog serve docs --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000``. ``--host ::`` selects IPv6, while the default remains loopback. The preview has no authentication or TLS, so we use network binding only where this sharing is intended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.8.rst:26
msgid "The `diagram chapter <https://insanai.github.io/guidedog/manual/topics/diagrams.html>`_ covers Graphviz and Typst together. The `Typst guide <https://insanai.github.io/guidedog/manual/howto/typst-diagrams.html>`_ explains every option, local imports, offline packages and migration from separate figure files. All six translated manuals include the new material. `GDS 0014 <https://insanai.github.io/guidedog/discussions/records/0014-typst-diagrams.html>`_ records the reviewed implementation. Every unpacked platform archive exercises SVG and PNG diagram generation with an empty PATH."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.9.rst:8
msgid "Guidedog 1.0.0-beta.9"
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.9.rst:11
msgid "We can now write musical scores directly in an RST or MyST ``lilypond`` directive without installing an external LilyPond binary. Guidedog's in-process reader, rational score model and native engraver produce outlined Bravura SVG or PNG figures for websites and multi-system PDF books. Up to four voices sound together on a staff, with local voice policies, ``\\shiftOn`` and its relatives, mixed-rest placement and stacked dynamics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.9.rst:17
msgid "Scores support captions, alternative text, figure references, adaptive dark-mode web rendering and system-level PDF page breaks. LilyPond 2.24 ``\\markup`` works in scripts, tempo and rehearsal marks and instrument or staff-group names, while Scheme, layout and embedded-score markup are refused with placed diagnostics. Score SVGs carry ``<title>`` and ``<desc>`` accessibility descriptions alongside localized musical summaries and native key-signature orthography across all nine built-in UI languages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.9.rst:21
msgid "``guidedog convert`` names an unengraved LilyPond score file in a sentence, and ``--lang`` translates Guidedog's own labels in HTML and PDF output. Built-in CLDR date formatting now covers Hindi and Korean alongside the other seven UI languages. Temporary layout buffers in ``gd-engrave`` reserve and release through ``Options::scratch``, and ``--untrusted`` builds engrave inline notation while refusing external ``.ly`` files and ``\\include``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../releases/1.0.0-beta.9.rst:25
msgid "The `music chapter <https://insanai.github.io/guidedog/manual/topics/music.html>`_ covers directives, polyphony, lyrics, markup and trust boundaries, and `teaches a four-bar melody from Beethoven's Joy theme <https://insanai.github.io/guidedog/manual/topics/music.html#learn-from-beethoven-s-joy-theme>`_. All six translated manuals, website editions and README files have been reviewed for native idiom and musical terminology. `GDS 0015 <https://insanai.github.io/guidedog/discussions/records/0015-lilypond-music.html>`_ records the accepted design and qualification evidence, and every unpacked platform archive exercises native music engraving with an empty PATH."
msgstr ""
